# PostHog overrides (issue #21).
#
# The Kiseki project token + host are baked into `src/lib/posthog.ts` as defaults
# — a PostHog project token is a PUBLIC client-side ingest key (it ships in the
# browser bundle by definition and grants no read access), the same posture as
# the Auth0 domain/client id in `src/lib/auth.ts`. A deploy therefore needs no
# extra build plumbing.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` only when you want to point a local checkout at
# a DIFFERENT PostHog project (e.g. testing a change without polluting the real
# one). Analytics is a no-op whenever the token is empty.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
